-ad-off-entitlement-status-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-complete\"],\n  \"reviewedScreenshotHashes\": [\"9750eb9a8f6ea9c9ac14d942a27b0faa67e23f9830a1833cfc0ed67ae7392bc5\", \"71000ff70ebe6759cff7d7ca2a23b48d0cf98f5a23b8c5bf57cfc1917816a039\", \"e095b55be4ff19c084a934d3ac52320d68233a395b9de2046c3e97226afa6605\", \"87808856a186b45e8ebb52068ebe93cc7d5359b1c332508b406c7c9ce959dac3\", \"046528158dd60039882a4d1fb9b538459a87d225772b49740670c548a54baaca\", \"805834950f43dd658c4ef8937ceed1dd950d13c0474baf8f31d617dfbe412271\", \"6ebcb8711e954620fff6507e8f09facc35d8fdf81f686e227e289a2ae0a2ceb1\", \"3b7540723f532a43a77fd2ec4ebab1411c795e8d14e4274765e9af1343d45ef9\", \"4716ecbd4f013521f4753a23e4d6480ab77dbc56e655453c5494dd6d91123992\", \"5c8fddd3d6cf6512060bf35e0057c06e21f5e9da9274b2cf2b6fb5da5e9cb2bc\", \"8636e8c94c9f2c1c9843c46173aa3174a0b57d0ba8f6d4de3314d1e56ba4aa90\", \"0ea7ca54c48809049a11aff22e6828fba2054e4b8d06c76f928ba5ff87bdd10b\", \"92cf18a0f65a174089ead66313feb88a6ae66bbda8b1563a3185b0c06aa23780\", \"2f04a57a2717475af95b9f9f01b25ee30aef4427c89deea986fca2007e623daa\", \"f1e0b6194eaefd9c5515f42bef6a06221c8dcb71ee9568452ae83baed3692830\", \"184e646ef87a439af92f440b422191cc26e86a906bf553ab285304e9db881009\", \"05bb28197a7ade8ce0e6227e3875f91682b3f9a2f95b6efe00d61a864bf61e98\", \"a6951a8087a7348bdd2fc1adb7966a1ff04c1f175fcc6098458691f2396f94cf\"],\n  \"reviewerType\": \"llm-vision-headless-cli\",\n  \"summary\": \"The action-state modals are the strongest part of this community: they carry genuinely specific ad-off content (\\\"ADO-1042, paid today at 2:10 PM, card ending 4242\\\", \\\"120.00 USD community plan, 96.00 USD utility allocation\\\", \\\"Suppressed: member ad-off entitlement active on the 4.99 USD monthly plan\\\"), and workflow identity is clear from their titles. The failure is concentrated in the complete states: every completion banner (\\\"Suppression verified\\\", \\\"Settlement recorded\\\", \\\"Receipt opened\\\") is sliced off by the bottom navigation bar so only a partial line of text is readable, and the two checkout workflows show no completion confirmation on screen at all — ad-off-member-checkout complete is visually indistinguishable from its own start state. A second systemic problem is copy: large blocks of body text are acceptance-criteria prose about the UI itself (\\\"Entitlement, receipt, renewal, restore action, and affected ad slots stay together without payment-screen context\\\") rather than product copy, and the start-state cards repeat one truncated subtitle, \\\"Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…\\\", across three differently-titled cards.\",\n  \"holisticQuestionAnswers\": [\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"context-state-legibility\",\n      \"question\": \"Across this community's workflows, is it always clear what workflow and what state (start/in-progress/complete) the user is looking at?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Workflow identity is legible on the action modals and on most complete states, which show a large tinted hero title (\\\"Ad suppression proof\\\", \\\"Ad-off settlement allocation\\\", \\\"Ad-off receipt history\\\"). State is not legible. Four of six complete states either clip the confirmation banner behind the bottom nav or omit it entirely: ad-suppression complete shows only the top half of \\\"Suppression verified\\\", settlement complete only the top half of \\\"Settlement recorded\\\", receipt-evidence complete only the top half of \\\"Receipt opened\\\", and both checkout complete states show no confirmation element whatsoever. Member-checkout start and member-checkout complete render the same hero title, same \\\"Ad-free account\\\" card, same \\\"Payer and scope / Member pays 4.99 USD/month for their account\\\" rows — a user handed those two frames could not tell which is the finished purchase. Start states are also compromised: community-checkout start, ad-suppression start and entitlement-status start all open mid-scroll with the workflow hero title scrolled off, so the only workflow cue is the generic \\\"Ad-Free Community\\\" app bar plus a partially visible card body.\",\n      \"score\": 34,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"ad-suppression complete: green banner at the very bottom edge reads only 'Suppression verified' with its lower half cut by the Home/Messages bar\",\n        \"settlement-utility complete: olive banner clipped to the single line 'Settlement recorded' with no amount or settlement ID visible\",\n        \"member-checkout complete is pixel-equivalent to member-checkout start: same 'Member ad-off checkout' hero and same 'Manage / Manage subscription, cancel, restore, retry, or open receipt' row, with no success affordance\",\n        \"community-checkout start opens scrolled past its title, first visible text is the card heading 'Ad-free controls'\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-complete\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screenReviews\": [\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The frame opens mid-scroll: the top edge cuts into the 'Ad-free controls' card and the workflow's own hero title is nowhere on screen, so 'Ad-Free Community' in the app bar is the only context. The card body — 'Confirm checkout status; purchase creates receipt evidence, activates entitlement, and leaves manage/cancel/restore actions available.' — is written as a test assertion, not as copy a buyer would read before paying; it never states the price, which the action modal reveals as 120.00 USD/month. Below it, two near-identical dark card shells ('Entitlement record' and 'Receipt history') carry the exact same truncated subtitle 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' and the same 'Tap for expanded view' / 'Ad-free account' chip pair, so they read as one template stamped twice. The primary CTA 'Start ad-free checkout' is rendered in flat grey with a slashed-circle (⊘) glyph, the same visual language used elsewhere for suppression, which makes an enabled purchase button look blocked.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A checkout entry screen anchored at the top with its own title, the 120.00 USD/month community plan price and covered-member scope stated inline, a clearly enabled primary CTA, and distinct entitlement/receipt cards each carrying their own real summary line.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Card heading 'Ad-free controls' is clipped by the top of the scroll viewport\",\n        \"'Change plan' secondary button with a right-arrow glyph\",\n        \"Primary CTA 'Start ad-free checkout' in low-contrast grey with a ⊘ icon\",\n        \"'Entitlement record' and 'Receipt history' cards both subtitled 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…'\",\n        \"Right-aligned 'Minimized' chips on both dark cards\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is it clear what workflow this is and that it is at its start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"First readable text is the card heading 'Ad-free controls'; no checkout title is on screen\",\n          \"why\": \"With the hero scrolled away, the user has to infer the workflow from a button label rather than read it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe actual community content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Confirm checkout status; purchase creates receipt evidence, activates entitlement, and leaves manage/cancel/restore actions available.'\",\n          \"why\": \"This enumerates what the UI must do rather than telling the admin what they are buying or what it costs.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are actions clearly actionable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Start ad-free checkout' drawn grey with a ⊘ slashed-circle icon\",\n          \"why\": \"A prohibition glyph plus muted fill on the primary action reads as disabled with no stated reason.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"9750eb9a8f6ea9c9ac14d942a27b0faa67e23f9830a1833cfc0ed67ae7392bc5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This is the best-performing frame of the set: the sheet is titled 'Community ad-off checkout' with a close X, and 'Payer and scope — Community admin pays 120.00 USD/month for eligible members.' is real, specific, admin-scoped copy that distinguishes this workflow from the member checkout. The problems are the surrounding rows. 'Payment — Payment method, renewal, utility allocation, and fee details are shown.' and 'Manage — Manage subscription, cancel, restore, retry, or open receipt.' describe what the screen displays instead of displaying it: no card brand, no renewal date, no fee amount appears, even though the receipt workflow proves the app has 'card ending 4242' available. The status chip 'Ad-free status active' with the caption 'Entitlement, receipt, renewal, restore action, and affected ad slots stay together without payment-screen context' is a requirement sentence surfaced to the user. Below, the second card 'Ad-free account controls' repeats the identical 'Ad-free account' and 'Receipt or settlement' rows that appear verbatim on five other modals in this community.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A checkout sheet showing the concrete payment method, next renewal date, itemised fee and utility split, and a live confirm-purchase action — not prose asserting those details are shown.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Sheet title 'Community ad-off checkout' with X close control\",\n        \"'Community admin pays 120.00 USD/month for eligible members.'\",\n        \"'Payment method, renewal, utility allocation, and fee details are shown.'\",\n        \"Second card 'Ad-free account controls' with 'Receipt or settlement' row listing 'settlement ID, utility allocation, audit status, correction, and rollback path'\",\n        \"No confirm/pay button visible in the frame\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does displayed text sound like real product copy?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Payment method, renewal, utility allocation, and fee details are shown.'\",\n          \"why\": \"It is a statement about the UI's contents rather than the contents themselves; a real checkout would print the card and date.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the workflow identifiable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Header 'Community ad-off checkout' plus 'Community admin pays 120.00 USD/month'\",\n          \"why\": \"Title and payer line together make the community-level checkout unambiguous.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"71000ff70ebe6759cff7d7ca2a23b48d0cf98f5a23b8c5bf57cfc1917816a039\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Labelled the complete state, but nothing on screen indicates a completed purchase. The frame shows the dimmed hero 'Community ad-off checkout' with the subtitle 'Confirm payer, amount, entitlement scope, payment method, renewal, receipt, and restore/manage option before checkout.' — the word 'before' explicitly frames this as pre-purchase — followed by the same 'Ad-free account' card that appeared in the action state, ending at 'Manage — Manage subscription, cancel, restore, retry, or open receipt.' No receipt ID, no confirmation banner, no timestamp, no 'purchase complete' language. The other four workflows at least surface a clipped green/olive/blue confirmation strip; here there is not even that. The hero title and subtitle are also rendered at very low contrast (muted indigo on dark indigo), which makes the one piece of workflow context on the screen hard to read.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A post-purchase confirmation showing the charged amount (120.00 USD), a receipt reference, entitlement activation and renewal date, and a link into receipt evidence.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Low-contrast hero 'Community ad-off checkout' with subtitle ending 'before checkout.'\",\n        \"'Ad-free status active' chip repeated from the action state\",\n        \"'Community admin pays 120.00 USD/month for eligible members.'\",\n        \"No success banner, receipt number, or completion timestamp anywhere in the frame\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can a viewer tell this is the completed state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Subtitle reads '...restore/manage option before checkout.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The only state language on screen describes the moment before purchase, contradicting the intended complete state.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is there any visible evidence the checkout succeeded?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Frame ends at 'Manage subscription, cancel, restore, retry, or open receipt.'\",\n          \"why\": \"No receipt, charge, or confirmation element is rendered, so completion is unevidenced.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"e095b55be4ff19c084a934d3ac52320d68233a395b9de2046c3e97226afa6605\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Opens mid-scroll with the description sentence already cut at the top ('Confirm ad suppression status, 4.99 USD plan amount, each eligible slot, no impression, and the entitlement that caused it.'), so the workflow hero is missing. That sentence is itself a checklist of what must be confirmed rather than a statement about this community's ads. The 'Settlement and utility…' card title is truncated mid-word, its subtitle truncated too ('You can read the current details without changing …'), and it exposes a 'Read only' pill next to 'Expand' without saying why the settlement is read-only here. The lower half of the screen is close to empty: a single collapsed 'Local package details' row with a chevron sits above roughly a third of a screen of blank navy, which reads as unfinished rather than deliberate whitespace. As on the other start frames, 'Verify ad suppression' is a grey pill carrying a ⊘ glyph.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A suppression entry point titled in-frame, listing the actual suppressed slots and the entitlement causing them, with the read-only state explained and no large dead region below the fold.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Top-clipped sentence beginning 'Confirm ad suppression status, 4.99 USD plan amount…'\",\n        \"'Restore ads' secondary button\",\n        \"'Verify ad suppression' grey CTA with ⊘ icon\",\n        \"Card title truncated to 'Settlement and utility…' with subtitle truncated to '…without changing …'\",\n        \"'Read only' pill with eye icon, no accompanying explanation\",\n        \"Collapsed 'Local package details' row followed by a large empty navy area\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is it clear why an action is restricted?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Read only' pill on the 'Settlement and utility…' card\",\n          \"why\": \"The card states the mode but gives no reason, so the user cannot tell whether it is permanent or unlocked elsewhere.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the visual density appropriate?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Blank region below 'Local package details' spanning roughly a third of the viewport\",\n          \"why\": \"Thin content where real suppression detail is expected reads as an unfinished screen.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"87808856a186b45e8ebb52068ebe93cc7d5359b1c332508b406c7c9ce959dac3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Content-wise the strongest modal in the community: 'Suppression decision' as the sheet title, and the 'Ad slot state' card names concrete placements with concrete causes — 'Top banner — Suppressed: member ad-off entitlement active on the 4.99 USD monthly plan.' and 'In-stream placement — Suppressed: no impression or click recorded.' plus 'No impression — Analytics records suppression, not an ad impression.' That is real, checkable product copy. Two problems. First, the whole sheet is skinned in a desaturated olive-green (header and page background) while every other surface in this community is indigo, and nothing on screen explains why suppression gets its own colour scheme; the muted green header also has weak contrast against the near-black body. Second, the sheet again ends in the boilerplate 'Ad-free account controls' card whose rows ('Entitlement scope, renewal or expiry, receipt link, restore/manage action, and affected ad slots are visible.') are identical to the ones on the checkout, entitlement, settlement and receipt modals, and the next row is already clipped to 'Top banner' at the frame edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A suppression-decision sheet with the per-slot reasons it already shows, in the community's accent colour, without the repeated generic controls card underneath.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Title 'Suppression decision' on an olive-green header\",\n        \"'No sponsored message right now' chip\",\n        \"'Top banner — Suppressed: member ad-off entitlement active on the 4.99 USD monthly plan.'\",\n        \"'Evidence — Receipt and entitlement link explain the suppression.'\",\n        \"Repeated 'Ad-free account controls' card with 'Receipt or settlement' row; next row clipped at 'Top banner'\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe actual suppression behaviour in this community?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Suppressed: no impression or click recorded.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Slot-by-slot cause and analytics consequence are stated concretely, which is what an audit view needs.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the visual treatment consistent with the community?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Olive-green header and background versus the indigo 'Ad-Free Community' app bar elsewhere\",\n          \"why\": \"The colour shift is unexplained but does not obscure meaning, so it is a minor inconsistency.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"046528158dd60039882a4d1fb9b538459a87d225772b49740670c548a54baaca\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The workflow reads clearly — hero 'Ad suppression proof' in green with a crossed-eye icon and a specific subtitle ('Verify the 4.99 USD monthly ad-free plan, which ad slots are suppressed, why no ad rendered…') — and the 'Ad slot state' card repeats the good per-slot copy. But the completion signal is broken: the green 'Suppression verified' banner appears only at the very bottom edge, with the text bisected by the light Home/Messages navigation bar so roughly the lower half of the glyph and letters is gone, and whatever detail follows the heading is entirely off-screen. The single element that distinguishes this frame from the start state is the one element that is clipped. The hero subtitle is also rendered in a dim green-on-navy that is noticeably harder to read than the white card text directly beneath it.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A verified state where the confirmation banner sits fully above the bottom navigation, showing what was verified, when, and the entitlement it was checked against.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Hero 'Ad suppression proof' with crossed-eye icon\",\n        \"Green banner 'Suppression verified' clipped horizontally by the bottom nav bar\",\n        \"'Top banner — Suppressed: member ad-off entitlement active on the 4.99 USD monthly plan.'\",\n        \"Low-contrast green subtitle text over the navy hero area\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completed state legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Only the top half of the words 'Suppression verified' is rendered above the nav bar\",\n          \"why\": \"The sole state marker is cut off, so completion is inferred rather than shown.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is there layout clipping?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Green banner intersects the white Home/Messages bar mid-glyph\",\n          \"why\": \"Content is drawn underneath a persistent chrome element rather than inset above it.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"805834950f43dd658c4ef8937ceed1dd950d13c0474baf8f31d617dfbe412271\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Another top-clipped start frame — 'Ad-free controls' is sheared at the viewport edge and the entitlement hero is scrolled away. The description 'Confirm subscription record, 4.99 USD plan amount, manage subscription, restore purchase, open receipt, or verify suppressed ad slots.' at least names the price, but is again phrased as a list of things to confirm. The two dark cards below, 'Receipt history' and 'Ad suppression', are visually identical shells — same 'Minimized' chip on the right, same 'Tap for expanded view' chip, same 'Ad-free account' chip, same 'Expand' button — and both carry the same truncated subtitle 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…', which tells the user nothing that distinguishes a receipt list from an ad-slot audit. The third card is clipped mid-chip at the bottom edge behind the nav bar. Both CTAs ('Manage plan', 'Manage entitlement') are muted grey, and 'Manage entitlement' again carries the ⊘ glyph.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An entitlement overview anchored at its title, showing scope, renewal date and status inline, with receipt and suppression cards each carrying their own distinct summary line.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"'Ad-free controls' heading clipped at the top of the scroll area\",\n        \"'Confirm subscription record, 4.99 USD plan amount, manage subscription, restore purchase, open receipt, or verify suppressed ad slots.'\",\n        \"'Receipt history' and 'Ad suppression' cards with identical chip sets and the identical subtitle 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…'\",\n        \"Bottom card clipped mid-chip behind the Home/Messages bar\",\n        \"'Manage entitlement' CTA in grey with ⊘ icon\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the cards visually differentiated by their content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Both cards read 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' under different titles\",\n          \"why\": \"Reusing one truncated subtitle across differently-purposed cards makes them read as generic shells.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the entitlement state shown?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Visible text names the 4.99 USD plan but no expiry or active/expired status\",\n          \"why\": \"The action modal has 'Active through Aug 30' but the entry screen omits it, so status is not legible here.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"6ebcb8711e954620fff6507e8f09facc35d8fdf81f686e227e289a2ae0a2ceb1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Titled 'Entitlement record', and the four detail rows are the most product-like in the set: 'Scope — Member-level ad-off for current account and communities at 4.99 USD monthly.', 'Expiration — Active through Aug 30, renews monthly.', 'Ad-free slots — Eligible sponsored slots are suppressed while active.', 'Restore — Restore purchase and manage plan remain available.' Scope, price, expiry and renewal cadence are all concrete. Two weaknesses: the 'Ad-free status active' chip caption is again the requirement sentence about things staying 'together without payment-screen context', which is internal language surfaced to users; and the sheet is padded out by the same duplicated 'Ad-free account controls' card seen on every other modal, whose next row is already clipped to 'Scope' at the bottom edge. The 'Restore' row states restore actions 'remain available' but no restore or manage button is present in the frame, so the copy promises an affordance the screen does not offer.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An entitlement detail sheet with the scope/expiry/renewal facts it already shows, plus the actual restore and manage controls it references, and no duplicated boilerplate card.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Sheet title 'Entitlement record'\",\n        \"'Member-level ad-off for current account and communities at 4.99 USD monthly.'\",\n        \"'Active through Aug 30, renews monthly.'\",\n        \"'Restore purchase and manage plan remain available.' with no button on screen\",\n        \"Duplicated 'Ad-free account controls' card, next row clipped at 'Scope'\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the entitlement state clear?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Active through Aug 30, renews monthly.'\",\n          \"why\": \"An explicit expiry plus renewal cadence makes the entitlement's status unambiguous.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Do the referenced actions exist on screen?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Restore purchase and manage plan remain available.' with no visible control\",\n          \"why\": \"Describing an available action without rendering it weakens actionability, though the sheet scrolls.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"3b7540723f532a43a77fd2ec4ebab1411c795e8d14e4274765e9af1343d45ef9\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The hero 'Ad-off entitlement record' with a shield-check icon does identify the workflow, and the card underneath carries the good specifics ('Active through Aug 30, renews monthly', 'Member-level ad-off for current account and communities at 4.99 USD monthly'). But as a complete state it is weak: the only thing below the card is a sliver of a blue banner at the very bottom, with its text entirely hidden behind the Home/Messages bar — not even a heading is readable, so this frame gives less completion evidence than the suppression or settlement complete states, which at least surface a partial heading. The hero title and its subtitle ('Open entitlement scope, 4.99 USD monthly amount, expiration, subscription state, restore option, receipt link, and ad-free member view.') are drawn in a dim slate-blue that is markedly lower contrast than the white card text below, and that subtitle is a feature checklist rather than a sentence a member would read.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A completed entitlement view whose confirmation banner is fully visible above the bottom navigation and states what was opened or confirmed and when.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Hero 'Ad-off entitlement record' with shield-check icon, low-contrast slate-blue text\",\n        \"'Scope — Member-level ad-off for current account and communities at 4.99 USD monthly.'\",\n        \"'Expiration — Active through Aug 30, renews monthly.'\",\n        \"A blue banner edge at the bottom with all of its text obscured by the nav bar\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is completion evidenced on screen?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Bottom banner shows only a coloured edge; no heading text is readable\",\n          \"why\": \"The state marker is entirely clipped, so the frame cannot be distinguished from a mid-workflow view.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the hero text legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Slate-blue subtitle 'Open entitlement scope, 4.99 USD monthly amount, expiration…' on navy\",\n          \"why\": \"Contrast between the hero text and the navy background is far weaker than the card text beneath it.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"4716ecbd4f013521f4753a23e4d6480ab77dbc56e655453c5494dd6d91123992\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The most content-starved frame in the set. It opens on the fragment '…the entitlement that caused it.' — a sentence whose beginning is scrolled off — so a settlement workflow is introduced by a dangling clause. The two visible controls, 'Restore ads' and the grey ⊘-marked 'Verify ad suppression', belong to the suppression workflow, not settlement; the only settlement affordance is inside a card whose title is truncated to 'Settlement and utility…' and whose subtitle is the same generic 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…' used on the entitlement and receipt cards elsewhere. No amount, no settlement ID, no period is shown even though the action modal has '120.00 USD community plan, 96.00 USD utility allocation' available. Below 'Local package details' roughly 40% of the screen is empty navy.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A settlement entry screen naming the period and amounts (120.00 USD plan / 96.00 USD utility), the settlement status, and a clearly primary 'Review settlement' action, without a dead lower half.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Top-clipped fragment '…the entitlement that caused it.'\",\n        \"'Restore ads' and grey '⊘ Verify ad suppression' controls, both suppression-oriented\",\n        \"Card title truncated to 'Settlement and utility…' with subtitle 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…'\",\n        \"'Review settlement' button demoted alongside 'Expand'\",\n        \"Large empty navy region beneath the collapsed 'Local package details' row\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does what is shown make sense for the settlement workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Primary visible CTA is 'Verify ad suppression', not a settlement action\",\n          \"why\": \"The most prominent control belongs to a different workflow, so persona/workflow scoping reads wrong.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is real settlement content present?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No amount, ID or period appears anywhere in the frame\",\n          \"why\": \"Settlement data exists in the action modal but none of it surfaces at the start state.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"5c8fddd3d6cf6512060bf35e0057c06e21f5e9da9274b2cf2b6fb5da5e9cb2bc\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Titled 'Settlement utility', and the financial rows are genuinely specific: 'Destination — Community utility fund receives June ad-off allocation.', 'Amount — 120.00 USD community plan, 96.00 USD utility allocation.', 'Ready — Settlement is ready for owner action and export.', 'Correction option — Admin can correct allocation before final settlement.' That is legible, checkable product content. Two issues. The sheet is skinned in a khaki/olive palette (header and background) unrelated to the indigo community accent and different again from the green used on the suppression sheet, so three different colour identities appear across one community's modals. And the 'Ready … for owner action and export' copy has no corresponding export or settle button visible in the frame, and the sheet then falls back into the same duplicated 'Ad-free account controls' boilerplate rows found on the checkout and entitlement modals, here retitled 'Settlement and audit'.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A settlement sheet with the destination/amount/status facts it already carries, in the community accent, plus the export and correct actions its copy promises.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Sheet title 'Settlement utility' on a khaki header\",\n        \"'Community utility fund receives June ad-off allocation.'\",\n        \"'120.00 USD community plan, 96.00 USD utility allocation.'\",\n        \"'Settlement is ready for owner action and export.' with no export control visible\",\n        \"Second card 'Settlement and audit' reusing the standard 'Ad-free account' / 'Receipt or settlement' rows\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the settlement state and amount legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'120.00 USD community plan, 96.00 USD utility allocation.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Gross amount, allocated amount and destination fund are all named, so the state is readable.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the visual identity consistent?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Khaki header here versus green on the suppression sheet and indigo elsewhere\",\n          \"why\": \"Three palettes across one community's modals is inconsistent, though each remains readable.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"8636e8c94c9f2c1c9843c46173aa3174a0b57d0ba8f6d4de3314d1e56ba4aa90\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Workflow identity is good — 'Ad-off settlement allocation' hero with a bank-building icon — and the card retains the real numbers ('120.00 USD community plan, 96.00 USD utility allocation', 'Community utility fund receives June ad-off allocation'). The completion evidence is again broken by layout: the olive 'Settlement recorded' banner is sliced by the Home/Messages bar, showing only the upper portion of the heading and none of the body that should carry the settlement ID or timestamp. For a money-movement workflow, a confirmation that cannot be fully read is the wrong thing to clip. The hero title and subtitle are olive-on-navy at low contrast, and the subtitle ('Confirm monthly revenue, platform fee, community utility allocation, settlement status, and audit/rollback option.') is once more a checklist of fields rather than product copy.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A recorded-settlement state with a fully visible confirmation carrying the settlement ID, recorded timestamp, funded amount and a link to the audit or rollback path.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Hero 'Ad-off settlement allocation' with bank icon in low-contrast olive\",\n        \"'120.00 USD community plan, 96.00 USD utility allocation.'\",\n        \"'Correction option — Admin can correct allocation before final settlement.'\",\n        \"Olive 'Settlement recorded' banner cut mid-text by the bottom nav bar\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the recorded state fully evidenced?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Settlement recorded' heading clipped by the white nav bar, no ID or timestamp visible\",\n          \"why\": \"A financial confirmation without a readable reference cannot be treated as production-grade evidence.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is there contradictory copy for a completed state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Admin can correct allocation before final settlement.' shown alongside 'Settlement recorded'\",\n          \"why\": \"Pre-final and recorded language sit adjacent, blurring which state the screen is in.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"0ea7ca54c48809049a11aff22e6828fba2054e4b8d06c76f928ba5ff87bdd10b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Unlike the other start frames this one is anchored at its hero, 'Member ad-off checkout', and the payer line 'Member pays 4.99 USD/month for their account.' correctly distinguishes it from the 120.00 USD community-paid variant — persona scoping is right. What undermines it is that the hero title and subtitle are drawn in a dim indigo-on-navy that is much lower contrast than the white card text below, and the card is already showing 'Ad-free status active' before any purchase has been made, which contradicts a start-of-checkout state. The rows are the meta-copy pattern again: 'Payment — Payment method, renewal, receipt, retry, and cancellation are shown.' asserts details are shown while showing none of them. No price total, card, or start-checkout button is visible in the frame; the next card is clipped to a bare edge behind the nav bar.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A member checkout start showing the 4.99 USD charge, the actual payment method, renewal date, and a visible purchase action, without an 'active' status chip preceding the purchase.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Hero 'Member ad-off checkout' in low-contrast indigo\",\n        \"'Member pays 4.99 USD/month for their account.'\",\n        \"'Ad-free status active' chip present before checkout\",\n        \"'Payment method, renewal, receipt, retry, and cancellation are shown.'\",\n        \"Next card clipped to a thin edge behind the Home/Messages bar\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the shown state match a start-of-checkout?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Ad-free status active' chip on a pre-purchase screen\",\n          \"why\": \"Declaring the entitlement already active before the checkout begins misstates the state.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is persona scoping correct for this workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Member pays 4.99 USD/month for their account.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Payer and amount correctly differ from the community-admin checkout, so scoping is right.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"92cf18a0f65a174089ead66313feb88a6ae66bbda8b1563a3185b0c06aa23780\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The sheet header 'Member ad-off checkout' plus 'Member pays 4.99 USD/month for their account.' and 'Entitlement — Member entitlement activates immediately.' make the workflow and its scope clear, and the immediate-activation line is a genuine product statement. Beyond that the sheet is thin for a payment surface: 'Payment — Payment method, renewal, receipt, retry, and cancellation are shown.' names five things without rendering any of them, there is no total, no card, no renewal date, and no confirm-purchase button in frame. The lower half is consumed by the 'Ad-free account controls' card whose two rows are byte-identical to those on the community-checkout, entitlement, suppression, settlement and receipt sheets, with a third row already clipped to 'Payer and scope' at the frame edge — so the second half of this sheet carries no member-specific information at all.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A member checkout sheet rendering the 4.99 USD total, the payment instrument, the first renewal date, and a confirm action, with the boilerplate controls card removed.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Sheet title 'Member ad-off checkout' with X close\",\n        \"'Member pays 4.99 USD/month for their account.'\",\n        \"'Member entitlement activates immediately.'\",\n        \"'Payment method, renewal, receipt, retry, and cancellation are shown.' with no such details rendered\",\n        \"'Ad-free account controls' card duplicated from other workflows, third row clipped at 'Payer and scope'\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does this look like a real checkout?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No total, card, or confirm button; only 'Payment method, renewal, receipt, retry, and cancellation are shown.'\",\n          \"why\": \"A payment sheet that describes payment details instead of presenting them is not production-grade.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is content on this sheet specific to the member workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Lower card rows are identical to the settlement and receipt sheets\",\n          \"why\": \"Roughly half the sheet is shared boilerplate carrying no member-checkout information.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"2f04a57a2717475af95b9f9f01b25ee30aef4427c89deea986fca2007e623daa\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This frame is visually indistinguishable from the member-checkout start frame: same 'Member ad-off checkout' hero, same subtitle ending 'before checkout.', same 'Ad-free status active' chip, same 'Member pays 4.99 USD/month for their account.' and same 'Manage — Manage subscription, cancel, restore, retry, or open receipt.' rows in the same positions. The only difference is a bare indigo card edge at the very bottom whose text is entirely hidden behind the Home/Messages bar — so nothing readable on this screen says a purchase completed. There is no receipt number (the app clearly has one: 'ADO-1042' appears in the receipt workflow), no charge confirmation, no activation timestamp. As evidence of a completed member checkout, this screen proves nothing.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A purchase-complete state showing the 4.99 USD charge confirmed, the receipt reference, when the entitlement activated, and next steps such as viewing the receipt or managing the plan.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Hero and subtitle identical to the start frame, ending 'before checkout.'\",\n        \"'Ad-free status active' chip in the same position as the start frame\",\n        \"'Member pays 4.99 USD/month for their account.'\",\n        \"Indigo card edge at the bottom with all text obscured by the nav bar\",\n        \"No receipt ID, charge confirmation, or completion timestamp anywhere\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can this frame be told apart from the start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Every readable element matches the start frame, including 'Manage subscription, cancel, restore, retry, or open receipt.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Two states rendering the same pixels above the fold means the complete state is not evidenced.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completion copy accurate?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Subtitle still reads '...restore/manage option before checkout.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The screen's own copy places the user before the purchase, contradicting the labelled state.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"f1e0b6194eaefd9c5515f42bef6a06221c8dcb71ee9568452ae83baed3692830\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The strongest start frame: the hero 'Ad-off receipt history' is visible and the card carries genuinely specific receipt content — 'Receipt — ADO-1042, paid today at 2:10 PM, card ending 4242.', 'Entitlement — Member ad-free entitlement active through Aug 30.', 'Export — Receipt can be exported with checksum and audit trail.' That is what real product copy looks like, and it is the only start state in this community that shows concrete transactional data. Two flaws: a black debug-looking strip labelled 'In-focus product surface' with an 'Expand' link is pinned across the top of the content area, which reads as instrumentation chrome rather than product UI; and the hero title/subtitle are again dim indigo on navy at noticeably lower contrast than the card text below. The card is also clipped at the bottom edge by the nav bar.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The same receipt list content without the 'In-focus product surface' instrumentation strip, with hero text at readable contrast and the card fully inset above the bottom navigation.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Black strip reading 'In-focus product surface' with 'Expand' at the top of the content area\",\n        \"Hero 'Ad-off receipt history' in low-contrast indigo\",\n        \"'ADO-1042, paid today at 2:10 PM, card ending 4242.'\",\n        \"'Member ad-free entitlement active through Aug 30.'\",\n        \"Card bottom edge clipped by the Home/Messages bar\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe actual community content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'ADO-1042, paid today at 2:10 PM, card ending 4242.'\",\n          \"why\": \"A concrete receipt ID, time and card suffix is exactly the specificity the other workflows lack.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is any non-product chrome visible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Strip labelled 'In-focus product surface' above the content\",\n          \"why\": \"This is scaffolding language, not something a member would ever be shown.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"184e646ef87a439af92f440b422191cc26e86a906bf553ab285304e9db881009\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Titled 'Receipt evidence' and carrying the sharpest content in the community: 'ADO-1042, paid today at 2:10 PM, card ending 4242.', 'Member ad-free entitlement active through Aug 30.', 'Receipt can be exported with checksum and audit trail.', 'Restore purchase uses this receipt and payer context.' Workflow, state and data are all unambiguous. The weaknesses are consistent with the rest of the set rather than unique: the 'Ad-free status active' chip caption is the internal 'stay together without payment-screen context' sentence, no export or download control is rendered despite the export copy, and the lower half repeats the identical 'Ad-free account controls' card ('Entitlement scope, renewal or expiry, receipt link…') with the following row already clipped to 'Receipt' at the frame edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A receipt detail sheet with the transaction facts it already shows plus a working export/download action, and without the shared boilerplate controls card.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Sheet title 'Receipt evidence' with X close\",\n        \"'ADO-1042, paid today at 2:10 PM, card ending 4242.'\",\n        \"'Receipt can be exported with checksum and audit trail.' with no export button\",\n        \"'Restore purchase uses this receipt and payer context.'\",\n        \"Duplicated 'Ad-free account controls' card, next row clipped at 'Receipt'\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the receipt content specific and real-sounding?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'ADO-1042, paid today at 2:10 PM, card ending 4242.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Identifier, timestamp and instrument together read as an actual transaction record.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are described actions available?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Export row present but no export control in frame\",\n          \"why\": \"The affordance is named but not offered, a minor actionability gap on an otherwise strong sheet.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"05bb28197a7ade8ce0e6227e3875f91682b3f9a2f95b6efe00d61a864bf61e98\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Workflow is clear from the 'Ad-off receipt history' hero and the card repeats the concrete 'ADO-1042, paid today at 2:10 PM, card ending 4242.' and 'Member ad-free entitlement active through Aug 30.' The completion marker fails the same way as the other complete states: the indigo 'Receipt opened' banner sits at the very bottom edge with its lower half cut by the Home/Messages bar and everything after the heading off-screen. 'Receipt opened' is also weak as a completion statement — it restates the navigation event rather than confirming an outcome, and it duplicates information already obvious from the receipt card directly above it. The hero subtitle ('Open receipt evidence with payer, amount, date, entitlement scope, payment state, refund option, and exportable audit record.') is a field checklist, and refund/export options it names appear nowhere on this frame.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A completed receipt view with a fully visible confirmation above the bottom navigation that states an outcome (exported, refunded, verified) rather than 'Receipt opened', plus the refund and export controls its subtitle promises.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Hero 'Ad-off receipt history' with receipt icon\",\n        \"Indigo banner 'Receipt opened' clipped mid-glyph by the bottom nav bar\",\n        \"'ADO-1042, paid today at 2:10 PM, card ending 4242.'\",\n        \"Subtitle names 'refund option' and 'exportable audit record' with no corresponding controls on screen\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completion banner readable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Receipt opened' text bisected by the white Home/Messages bar\",\n          \"why\": \"Only the top half of the heading renders and its supporting line is entirely off-screen.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the banner describe a meaningful completion?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Receipt opened' above a card already showing the full receipt\",\n          \"why\": \"It restates the navigation rather than confirming an outcome, adding no information.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"a6951a8087a7348bdd2fc1adb7966a1ff04c1f175fcc6098458691f2396f94cf\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"complete-state-not-evidenced-on-checkouts\",\n      \"title\": \"Both checkout workflows show no completion evidence; member checkout complete is identical to its start\",\n      \"description\": \"ad-off-community-checkout complete and ad-off-member-checkout complete render the same hero, subtitle ('...restore/manage option before checkout.'), 'Ad-free status active' chip and 'Payer and scope' rows as their pre-purchase frames. The member checkout complete frame is visually indistinguishable from the member checkout start frame above the fold; its only differing element is a bare card edge fully hidden behind the bottom navigation. No receipt reference, charged amount confirmation, or activation timestamp is visible on either screen, even though the receipt workflow demonstrates that a real receipt ID ('ADO-1042') exists in this data.\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Render a distinct post-purchase state for both checkouts showing the confirmed charge (120.00 USD / 4.99 USD), the receipt reference, entitlement activation and renewal date, and update the hero subtitle so it no longer says 'before checkout'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"completion-banners-clipped-by-bottom-nav\",\n      \"title\": \"Every completion banner is sliced by the Home/Messages navigation bar\",\n      \"description\": \"'Suppression verified' (ad-suppression complete), 'Settlement recorded' (settlement complete) and 'Receipt opened' (receipt complete) all render at the extreme bottom of the viewport with their glyphs bisected by the opaque white bottom navigation bar, and their supporting body text entirely off-screen. On entitlement-status complete only a coloured card edge is visible with no readable text at all. In each case the single element that marks the state is the element that is clipped, and for the settlement workflow this hides money-movement details such as the settlement ID.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Scroll or inset the complete states so the confirmation banner and its detail line render fully above the bottom navigation, and include the outcome specifics (ID, amount, timestamp) in the banner body.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"requirement-prose-instead-of-product-copy\",\n      \"title\": \"Body copy asserts what the UI shows instead of showing it\",\n      \"description\": \"Across every modal the detail rows are acceptance-criteria sentences rather than product copy: 'Payment — Payment method, renewal, utility allocation, and fee details are shown.' (community checkout), 'Payment method, renewal, receipt, retry, and cancellation are shown.' (member checkout), and the status chip caption 'Entitlement, receipt, renewal, restore action, and affected ad slots stay together without payment-screen context.' which appears on seven screens. Hero subtitles follow the same pattern ('Confirm payer, amount, entitlement scope, payment method, renewal, receipt, and restore/manage option before checkout.'). The result is that payment surfaces name a card, a renewal date and a fee without ever rendering any of them, while the receipt workflow proves those values exist ('card ending 4242').\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Replace the 'X, Y and Z are shown' rows with the actual values (payment instrument, renewal date, fee breakdown) and rewrite the status chip caption as user-facing copy about the entitlement, not about screen composition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"duplicated-card-shells-and-truncated-subtitles\",\n      \"title\": \"Repeated generic card shells and one truncated subtitle reused across differently-purposed cards\",\n      \"description\": \"On the start screens, 'Entitlement record', 'Receipt history', 'Ad suppression' and 'Settlement and utility…' cards all share the identical chrome — right-aligned 'Minimized' chip, 'Tap for expanded view' chip, 'Ad-free account' chip, 'Expand' button — and all carry the same truncated subtitle 'Ad preference and sponsored-message beh…', which conveys nothing distinguishing. Card titles themselves truncate mid-phrase ('Settlement and utility…'). On the action modals, an identical 'Ad-free account controls' card with byte-identical 'Ad-free account' and 'Receipt or settlement' rows is appended to the community-checkout, member-checkout, entitlement, suppression, settlement and receipt sheets, consuming the lower half of each with no workflow-specific content.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-member-checkout-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-action\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Give each card its own summary line drawn from its own data (latest receipt, suppressed slot count, settlement period), stop truncating card titles, and remove or heavily condense the duplicated 'Ad-free account controls' block on the modals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"start-frames-open-mid-scroll\",\n      \"title\": \"Start states open scrolled past their titles, some on a dangling sentence fragment\",\n      \"description\": \"community-checkout start opens with the 'Ad-free controls' heading already sheared at the viewport top; entitlement-status start does the same; ad-suppression start opens mid-sentence on 'Confirm ad suppression status, 4.99 USD plan amount…'; settlement-utility start opens on the fragment '…the entitlement that caused it.' with no settlement heading anywhere on screen. In each case the workflow hero is scrolled away, leaving the generic 'Ad-Free Community' app bar as the only context cue, and on settlement start the most prominent control on screen ('Verify ad suppression') belongs to a different workflow entirely.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Anchor each start state at the top of its workflow so the hero title and full description are visible, and ensure the workflow's own primary action is the prominent control on its start screen.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"empty-lower-half-on-suppression-and-settlement-start\",\n      \"title\": \"Large empty regions below the fold on two start screens\",\n      \"description\": \"ad-suppression start and settlement-utility start both end in a single collapsed 'Local package details' row with a chevron, below which roughly a third to 40% of the viewport is blank navy with no content. On settlement start in particular no amount, settlement ID or period appears anywhere, despite '120.00 USD community plan, 96.00 USD utility allocation' being available one tap away in the action modal.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Populate the lower area with the real suppression slot list and settlement summary (period, gross, allocated amount, status) instead of leaving dead space under a collapsed row.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"prohibition-glyph-on-primary-ctas\",\n      \"title\": \"Primary CTAs render grey with a slashed-circle glyph, reading as disabled\",\n      \"description\": \"'Start ad-free checkout', 'Verify ad suppression', 'Manage entitlement', 'Open receipt' and 'Review settlement' are all drawn as low-contrast grey pills prefixed with a ⊘ slashed-circle icon — the same prohibition glyph used elsewhere in the community as the ad-off mark. On a primary purchase or verification button this reads as blocked or unavailable, and no explanatory text accompanies it. The result is that no start screen presents an obviously enabled primary action.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-community-checkout-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-start\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Give enabled primary actions filled accent styling and drop the slashed-circle glyph from actionable buttons; reserve it for genuinely suppressed or disabled states, which should carry a reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"inconsistent-modal-palettes-and-low-contrast-heroes\",\n      \"title\": \"Three different modal palettes and low-contrast hero text\",\n      \"description\": \"The suppression sheet uses a desaturated green header and background, the settlement sheet a khaki/olive one, while checkout, entitlement and receipt sheets stay indigo — three colour identities within one community with no explanation. Separately, on every complete state the hero title and subtitle are tinted versions of the accent drawn directly on navy ('Ad-off entitlement record' in slate-blue, 'Ad-off settlement allocation' in olive, 'Ad suppression proof' subtitle in dim green), giving noticeably weaker contrast than the white card text immediately beneath.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-action\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-entitlement-status-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-settlement-utility-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-complete\", \"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Standardise modal chrome on the community accent and raise hero title/subtitle contrast against the navy background to match the legibility of the card body text.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"instrumentation-strip-visible-in-product\",\n      \"title\": \"'In-focus product surface' scaffolding strip rendered above product content\",\n      \"description\": \"On ad-off-receipt-evidence start a black bar reading 'In-focus product surface' with an 'Expand' link sits pinned across the top of the content area, directly above the 'Ad-off receipt history' hero. This is harness/instrumentation language rather than anything a community member would be shown.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-receipt-evidence-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Remove the 'In-focus product surface' strip from rendered product screens, or hide it outside capture/debug builds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"unexplained-read-only-state\",\n      \"title\": \"'Read only' pill shown without a reason\",\n      \"description\": \"On ad-off-ad-suppression start the 'Settlement and utility…' card exposes a 'Read only' pill with an eye icon next to 'Expand', and its truncated subtitle 'You can read the current details without changing …' cuts off before explaining anything. The user cannot tell whether the settlement is permanently read-only, read-only because of their role, or unlockable from the settlement workflow.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"ad-free-community-ad-off-ad-suppression-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"State the reason the settlement card is read-only in this context and point to where the editable view lives, rather than showing an unqualified 'Read only' pill with truncated explanatory text.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":18888,"ttft_stream_ms":17933,"time_to_request_ms":16768,"type":"result","duration_ms":418179,"uuid":"f1c2bd4c-a0e0-484e-a195-7df8060b8398"}
